    "Model exhibits severe downward bias when recent history shows a sharp decline (e.g., dropping from ~89 to ~77) followed by high volatility; forecasts often predict continued low levels while true outcomes rebound sharply.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture mean reversion after extreme lows, systematically underestimating the recovery phase by 10-20 EUR over a 30-day horizon.",
    "Sentiment history (values > 0.20) appears disconnected from price action in these examples; model ignores sentiment spikes that precede or accompany sudden price surges.",
    "Model displays excessive smoothing and lag, predicting flat or slowly rising paths instead of the high-frequency oscillations seen in true outcomes.",
    "When recent history ends near a local minimum (e.g., 77.50), the model predicts further decline or stagnation, whereas true outcomes consistently reverse direction within 3-5 days."
